  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Thursday)\nIssued at 1155 AM CDT FRI OCT 16 2026\n\nA strong cold front is expected to move through the area today.\nWinds are already shifting to the NW in NW portions of AL here\naround noon. We're not expecting much in the way of rainfall with\nthis, though a few sprinkles can't be ruled out. The main impact\nis going to be gusty winds this afternoon and through much of the\nday tomorrow as the front moves through. This will be some of the\ncoldest temperatures so far this year with lows Saturday dropping\ninto the upper 40s to near 50, then dropping to the low to mid\n40s on Sunday and Monday mornings. Daytime highs should rebound\nquite a bit, reaching the upper 60s to low 70s for overall mild\nFall conditions this weekend.\n\nThis trough that's moving through develops into a cut-off low\nalong the Atlantic Coast Sunday into Monday as ridging builds in\nto our west. This will generally lead to continued dry weather\nwith northerly to northwesterly flow. We'll gradually see a\nwarming trend through the remainder of the week with mostly clear\nskies and ample sunshine, though overnight lows will remain in\nthe mid to upper 40 to near 50 through Friday.\n\n25/Owen",
